spans.s:
विभक्त a. divided, separated by (instr. & —˚) or from
(instr.), isolated, lonely;
 distinct, different, manifold;
 regular,
symmetrical. n. separation, isolation, loneliness.

विभङ्ग m. bending, contracting (of the eye-brows);
incision, furrow;
 interruption, disturbance, frustration.

विभव a. rich. m. omnipresence, ubiquity,
[]
evolution, development, growth;
 power, might, majesty, rank, high
position;
 property, wealth, money.

विभाग॑ m. distribution, apportionment, division,
partition, esp. of an inheritance;
 share, portion, part;
 separation,
distinction, difference.

विभावन a. & n. developing, manifesting;
 n. also
perceiving, ascertaining;
 f. आ a cert. rhetor. figure.

†विभावरी adj. f. to विभा॑वन्;
 f. the star-light
night, night i.g.

विभी॑तक m. N. of a tree;
 n. its nut (used for
dicing).

विभी॑दक m. N. of a tree;
 n. its nut (used for
dicing).

विभी॑षण a. terrifying, horrible. m. N. of a Rākṣasa
etc.;
 n. frightening, terror.

विभु॑ f. विभू॑ & विभ्वी॑ far-reaching, pervading,
omnipresent;
 abundant, intense, powerful, mighty, able to (infin). m.
lord, ruler, chief of (—˚), E. of Brahman, Viṣṇu, & Śiva;
 N. of a
god etc.

विभू॑ f. विभू॑ & विभ्वी॑ far-reaching, pervading,
omnipresent;
 abundant, intense, powerful, mighty, able to (infin). m.
lord, ruler, chief of (—˚), E. of Brahman, Viṣṇu, & Śiva;
 N. of a
god etc.

विभेद m. breaking, splitting, piercing;
 bending,
contracting (of the eyebrows), change, alteration;
 interruption,
disturbance;
 falling asunder, decay;
 discord, difference.

विभ्रम m. unsteady motion, flurry, going to and fro,
esp. of the eyes;
 coquetry, grace, beauty;
 confusion, agitation, error,
mistake;
 erroneous application of (gen.);
 mistaking for, phantom or mere
semblance of (—˚).

विभ्रष्ट a. fallen, ruined;
 separated from, deprived
of, thwarted in (—˚);
 idle, vain;
 vanished, gone.

विभ्वतष्ट॑ a. fashioned by Vibhvan or by a skilful
artificer;
 well made, perfect.
